				// We'll try to process line if it looks complete for closing; otherwise EOF error.
				// Fall through with line handling, marking EOF.
				// For simplicity, if line doesn't end with \n, return EOF error like "failed to read header: EOF"
				// but first check closing/stanza cases are handled by callers? Use generic:
				return nil, hdrErr("parsing age header: failed to read header: EOF")
